orted, rules already present).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-4bfafab2f49f4dd4\",\"cmd-fc7cde996f0a4070\"]},{\"id\":\"persistent\",\"requirement\":\"Firewall configuration is persistent (survives reload/reboot, not just runtime)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Rules applied with permanent:true / firewall-cmd --permanent. Direct rule set (INPUT_direct chain) verified identical after `firewall-cmd --reload` (cmd-3a42d990961f48c0) and after a full node1 reboot with changed boot_id (cmd-138928a20f654e34 baseline -> cmd-3fd9e9b30ad44107 changed boot id -> cmd-9068f8306876481a showing rules intact), plus live functional re-tests post-reboot for all three sources.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-3a42d990961f48c0\",\"cmd-138928a20f654e34\",\"cmd-3fd9e9b30ad44107\",\"cmd-9068f8306876481a\",\"cmd-92131da9aeba4a5f\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.75,\"summary\":\"Executor iterated through several failed configuration approaches before landing on the working solution: (1) an initial rich-rule playbook that misordered accept/reject (cmd-9425bcdc6b044453, retained until superseded), (2) a rich-rule 'priority' attribute attempt that failed outright with no state change (cmd-82e76a3619c549cb), (3) an attempt using unsupported 'direct'/'tuple' firewalld module params that failed with no state change (cmd-2748e33697cf481c). All of these were cleanly superseded by the final direct-rule playbook (cmd-4bfafab2f49f4dd4), which explicitly disables the earlier rich rules before adding the working INPUT_direct rules, so no conflicting rules were left behind. Ad hoc test HTTP listeners (python2 SimpleHTTPServer on port 9000) were started multiple times for verification (cmd-5fe6f03584a14f22, cmd-7349e807b3b34a16, cmd-1ba72cd3253b4c0b, cmd-3b4e31b754b14bf0) and each was killed afterward (cmd-d160b26cf42445b1, cmd-55dd9b5e6f234d44, cmd-38c22f3aad644c52, cmd-000a9eab3bb24b94) — bounded, low-risk, and fully reverted, though their log/pid files (/tmp/httpsrv*.log, /tmp/h